&lt;p&gt;At Tines, we&#39;re driven by our values of Simplicity, Speed, and Soundness. We&#39;re committed to delivering exceptional customer experiences while fostering a company culture that nurtures individual curiosity, growth, and integrity. We’re excited about what’s next, and we’re looking for others to join us on our journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tines is investing in its quote-to-cash platform and process. This role contributes to how that platform is built and administered. You will be the systems owner for our quote-to-cash configuration in DealHub and Salesforce, inputting to the design direction, and technical build and administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own DealHub build-out, configuration and day-to-day admin.&lt;/strong&gt; Be the accountable owner of the platform: product catalog and SKU architecture, pricing and discounting rules, playbooks and quote flows, approval workflows, document and template management, and the Salesforce integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to the platform roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt; Working with Senior team members, translate where the business is going into a sequenced buildout plan as our products and commercial models evolve, and make the design calls that keep the configuration extensible rather than accumulating rework with every pricing change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support our implementation partners.&lt;/strong&gt; Scope and prioritise third-party services work, translate their the specifications and execute the builds, review and test what comes back, and hold quality and timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set standards and governance.&lt;/strong&gt; Define how change gets made: intake and prioritisation, sandbox and release practice, testing expectations, documentation standards, and the data-quality rules that stop bad data being created at the point of entry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the wider GTM stack in your scope.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain Salesforce configuration (objects, fields, flows, validation rules, permission sets, reporting) and the adjacent GTM tools that integrate with quote-to-cash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the systems partner to the business.&lt;/strong&gt; Run requirements discovery with Sales, Deal Desk, Finance, and Legal, push back when an ask will not scale, and turn ambiguous business problems into specs people can build from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain standards.&lt;/strong&gt; Create the documentation and delivery standards for GTM Systems, mentor more junior analysts as the team grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in GTM systems, business systems analysis, revenue systems, or sales operations in a B2B SaaS environment, including ownership of a revenue-critical platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on DealHub administration experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You have configured, not just used, DealHub: product catalog, pricing and discount rules, playbooks, approval workflows, templates, and the CRM integration. This is a requirement for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Salesforce administration fluency: objects, fields, flows, validation rules, permission sets, reports and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of quote-to-cash: quoting, approvals, order forms, amendments, renewals, and the downstream handoffs into billing and compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated solution design, not just configuration: you can take an ambiguous business problem, choose an approach, and defend the trade-offs behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scoping and managing external implementation partners or contractors, and holding them to a standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence advising and influencing senior stakeholders, including saying no to a request that will not scale, and settling disagreements across Sales, Finance, and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication with both technical and non-technical audiences, and a service mindset toward the reps who depend on the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to a second enterprise CPQ platform alongside DealHub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience configuring CPQ through a pricing or packaging change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside external implementation partners or systems integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to CaptivateIQ, NetSuite, or comparable ICM and ERP integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Administrator or Platform App Builder certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile or sprint-based delivery model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;$126k- 150k OTE + equity&lt;/p&gt;
