&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Lead Customer Success Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the post-sales strategic relationship, retention, and value realization across our highest-stakes enterprise accounts. You are a self-starter and bar-raiser who operates with high autonomy, driving customer outcomes while working in tight partnership with Sales to uncover and capitalize on strategic growth opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will serve as the trusted advisor and strategic lead for your portfolio, orchestrating technical and commercial counterparts—including Forward-Deployed Engineers (FDEs), Account Executives, and Product leaders. You will bridge complex technical deployments with executive-level business goals, ensuring customers realize maximum value from their investment and naturally expand their footprint with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Strategic Account Value &amp;amp; Retention:&lt;/strong&gt; Accountable for net retention, customer health, and long-term strategic alignment across a portfolio of complex enterprise accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Sales for Account Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Work side-by-side with Account Executives/Strategic Account Managers to identify expansion vectors, co-develop account plans, and position new capabilities that directly support the customer&#39;s technical roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrate with Technical Counterparts:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with &lt;strong&gt;Forward-Deployed Engineers (FDEs)&lt;/strong&gt; and technical leads to ensure technical delivery aligns directly with the client&#39;s business outcomes, removing friction and accelerating time-to-value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operate as an Independent Bar-Raiser:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively build scalable Customer Success playbooks, elevate executive engagement standards, and operate with extreme ownership without needing step-by-step guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultivate C-Suite &amp;amp; Technical Sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Build multi-threaded relationships across business and technology functions (CIO, CISO, CTO, VPs of Engineering, Product Leads) to ensure continuous alignment with top corporate initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Business Outcomes &amp;amp; QBRs:&lt;/strong&gt; Shift client conversations from product usage to business impact, leading executive business reviews (EBRs/QBRs) that demonstrate clear ROI and anchor the account for long-term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Sales Strategic Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years in Enterprise Customer Success, Account Management, or Technical Account Management handling high-ARR, complex enterprise platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Acumen &amp;amp; Growth Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven history of partnering with Sales to identify, nurture, and help close upsells, expansions, and renewals in complex, multi-stakeholder environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical &amp;amp; FDE Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep experience collaborating with Forward-Deployed Engineers, Solutions Architects, and product delivery teams to translate technical achievements into commercial value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Autonomy &amp;amp; Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Self-motivated bar-raiser with a bias for action who excels in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and takes full accountability for account outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Outstanding communication and presentation skills, with a track record of challenging and advising C-level executives on technology strategy and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves / Pluses&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Tech Industry Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Domain knowledge in High Tech (e.g., cloud native, hardware/software OEMs, or AI/ML platforms) and an understanding of how engineering-led enterprises operate and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like in Year 1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Month 3:&lt;/strong&gt; Fully onboarded, account health assessments completed, and tight alignment established with assigned Sales AEs and FDE teams on key accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Month 6:&lt;/strong&gt; Value-realization frameworks and executive cadence active across all accounts, with clear expansion pipelines co-developed alongside Sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Month 12:&lt;/strong&gt; High Net Retention Rate (NRR) achieved across the portfolio, demonstrable business outcomes delivered with FDEs, and elevated CS playbooks established as standard practice for the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Annual Earnings (salary + commission): $190K-220K OTE (80/20 split)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
